From b439fafd4237c5709e714a8cf045b7c529c64c0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:12:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(web-scan): re-check RPC-failed router claims once
 from a capped list; flag large head drops

Review of 2642db3 on #70: the rewind rule (hold the checkpoint at a recheck
claim strictly after the run start) lost a payment whenever the run start
itself landed on the claim block (pending rule, replay tail, budget stop,
typed Start block), and k always-failing spam claims slowed the cursor to
one block per run.

- persistable(): the rewind rule is removed; the cursor advances as before
  round 1 (pending rule, floor and corroboration unchanged).
- ScanCursor gains recheck?: readonly bigint[] (sorted, unique, < nextBlock,
  at most RECHECK_MAX = 8): blocks of this run's main-scan claims marked
  recheck, capped to the 8 lowest. More than that returns recheckOverflow
  { count, fromBlock }, shown in the Scan view through the new critical key
  scan.recheck.overflow (en source, es/ja/ar machine drafts).
- runScan first re-reads each owed block alone (same announcer/router
  filters, second-provider reconciliation, worker matching and
  verifyClaimedPayment path) and merges the results by announcement id.
  Abortable, bounded by RECHECK_MAX single-block reads, errors drop the
  block, and a retried block is never carried forward again.
- localCheckpointStore persists recheck as decimal strings; old checkpoints
  load unchanged and a malformed list is dropped on load while the rest of
  the checkpoint is kept.
- verifyClaimedPayment marks head skew retryable: both providers received
  with the same evidenceId, binding and evidence, differing only in final.
- Head telemetry also tracks the highest page head; a later page head more
  than finalityDepth below it marks the privacy set partial.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
